The '''2017 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2017 FIFA Club World Cup]], the 14th edition of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised [[association football|football]] tournament contested by the winners of the six continental confederations, as well as the host nation's league champions. The final was played at the [[Zayed Sports City Stadium]] in [[Abu Dhabi]], United Arab Emirates on 16 December 2017 and was contested between [[Royal Spanish Football Federation|Spanish]] club and title holders [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]], representing [[UEFA]] as the reigning champions of the [[UEFA Champions League]], and [[Brazilian Football Confederation|Brazilian]] club [[Grêmio Foot-Ball Porto Alegrense|Grêmio]], representing [[CONMEBOL]] as the reigning champions of the [[Copa Libertadores]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://resources.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/02/87/91/93/fcwc2017_matchschedule_30112017_neutral.pdf |title=Match Schedule – FIFA Club World Cup UAE 2017 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |format=PDF |year=2017 |access-date=12 December 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171215054028/http://resources.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/02/87/91/93/fcwc2017_matchschedule_30112017_neutral.pdf |archive-date=15 December 2017 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref>

Real Madrid won the match 1–0 via a goal from [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] for their third FIFA Club World Cup title. This was the first time a team had successfully defended the FIFA Club World Cup title, after Real won the [[2016 FIFA Club World Cup|previous year]]. The victory also marked the tenth time a UEFA team had won the Club World Cup.

